Third-Party Data

This software can optionally import and use product data from Open Food
Facts (https://world.openfoodfacts.org). That data is made available under
the Open Database License (ODbL) v1.0:
https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/

When the nutrition module is enabled and a local copy of the Open
Food Facts database is imported, scanned products are enriched with data
from Open Food Facts. Items enriched this way are tagged with
`off_enriched: true` in their metadata and attributed in the UI.

The repository itself carries a small piece of that data: the evaluation
corpus `backend/scripts/vision_matrix_corpus.json` lists 14 Open Food Facts
barcodes with the product names and brands read off the packs (ODbL data,
attributed in the file). The photographs it points to are not in the
repository; the evaluation script fetches them from Open Food Facts at run
time, and Open Food Facts publishes its product images under CC-BY-SA.
